---
import ArticleClosingNote from '@/components/articles/ArticleClosingNote.astro';

const prose = 'article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0';
---

<section id="section-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">How I Experienced Bali Belly</h2>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>In my case, the symptoms didn't appear as soon as I arrived in Bali. They started around ten days into my trip, shortly after I began ordering green salads as a side with my meals.</p>
    <p>At first, the symptoms were mild, but by the third day they had become much worse. I visited a local pharmacy, where I bought activated charcoal tablets. They helped me recover, and from that day on, I completely stopped eating raw salads. I stayed in Bali for almost two months after that and didn't experience Bali Belly again.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">Can You Prevent Bali Belly?</h2>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>While there's no way to completely prevent Bali Belly, taking probiotics before and during your trip, washing your hands regularly, drinking bottled water (including when brushing your teeth), and being mindful of food and water can help reduce the risk.</p>
    <p>These simple precautions won't guarantee that you won't get Bali Belly, but they can help lower your chances.</p>
    <p>That said, every traveller is different, so even if you do everything "right", there's still a chance you could experience it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class={prose}>
    <ArticleClosingNote label="Before you go">
      <p>Just because someone had a bad experience with ice, salads, or any other food in Bali doesn't mean the same thing will happen to you. Everybody reacts differently, and that's always worth remembering.</p>
      <p>As a pharmacist, I always keep that in mind whenever I travel outside Europe. During the first few days, I pay a little more attention to what I eat so I can understand how my body reacts before trying everything. It's a simple habit that's helped me on many trips, and one I'd recommend if you're visiting Bali for the first time.</p>
    </ArticleClosingNote>
  </div>
</section>
